issue.body:
**Potential Bug**:
The string `"1"` results in query param value `true`:

``` js
this.router.navigate([
    '/UserList',
    {page: '1'}
]);

// --> /users/?page      (actual)
// --> /users/?page=1  (expected)
```

**Question**:
_Update: Duplicate of https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/2959_.
Is it intended that more complex query params aren't supported? Example:

``` js
this.router.navigate([
    '/UserList',
    {
        filtering: {
            name: 'Andrew',
            age: 22
        }
    }
]);

// --> /users/?filtering=[object%20Object]                 (actual)
// --> /users/?filtering[name]=Andrew&filtering[age]=22  (expected)
```
